{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Abraham rose up, etc., and he spoke to the children of Heth.</b> The men of the place were the children of Heth, and thus it is written (Genesis 10:15): ״וכנען ילד את צידן בכורו ואת חת״, and they are all children of Canaan. Scripture teaches us proper conduct, that one who speaks before many must stand; and so it returns below: ״ויקם אברהם וידבר אתם לאמר״." "<b>And it appears</b> that the custom was that when an individual speaks before many, he speaks standing, and when he finishes speaking he sits in his place. And so Abraham spoke standing, and said: ״גר ותושב אנכי עמכם״; and afterward he sat in his place, and the children of Heth answered him: ״שמענו אדוני נשיא אלהים אתה״. And when he wished to speak a second time, he stood and spoke; therefore he needed to rise a second time: ״ויקם אברהם״." "And as for what he said, <b>from before his dead</b> — and she was a female — it is because the body is masculine in gender, and what dies of the human being is the body, not the soul, for it exists eternally."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:14:19.475762213Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}